# Cargo build output
/target/

# Agent scratch space and local work logs (session-local, not part of the project).
# NOTE: .workbuddy-ai/skills/ is deliberately NOT ignored — project-level skills
# are meant to be shareable with the rest of the team.
.workbuddy-ai/tmp/
.workbuddy-ai/memory/

# NOTE: vendor/ must NEVER be ignored.
#
# Cargo.toml declares `[patch.crates-io] gpui = { path = "vendor/gpui" }`, i.e. a
# PATH dependency. Three local fixes live only there (all marked `LOCAL PATCH`):
#
#   vendor/gpui/src/window.rs  — stops gpui from re-presenting the cached scene on
#                                every vsync tick for a second after the last input
#                                event. Without it a focused but idle window replays
#                                the whole scene 60-144x per second (~20% GPU).
#   vendor/gpui/build.rs       — finds fxc.exe by scanning the installed Windows SDK
#                                versions. Without it `cargo build --release` panics
#                                with "Failed to find fxc.exe".
#   vendor/gpui/src/taffy.rs   — annotates the `0.0`/`1.0` grid-track literals as
#                                `f32`. They cannot be inferred (no `From<f64> for
#                                f32`) and fall back to `f32` only via the
#                                `float_literal_f32_fallback` `future_incompatible`
#                                lint, which will become a hard error.
#
# If vendor/gpui is missing, the build fails for everyone, so it has to be committed.
# Do make sure no stray target/ sneaked into it (registry copies sometimes carry one).
